# Firstmall Skin Integration Rules

## Original Skin Baseline

Compare `firstmall-workskin/` against this folder only. Never edit it.

`C:\Users\user\Desktop\(DONT CHANGE-20260730)Firstmall-original\responsive_food_mealkit_gl`

- File exists there → **수정** / missing there → **신규**
- Do not use git status for that classification.

## Pre-Edit Checklist (mandatory)

Before changing any work-skin HTML/JS, open the **same path** in the original skin and check:

1. **Includes / modules** — `#subpageLNB`, `{#board_lnb}`, `{#form_member}`, `<!-- [스킨폴더]/… -->`, layout header/footer. Edit the **owning module**; do not paste its markup into every page.
2. **Template tokens** — keep `{members…}`, `{member…}`, `{#paging}`, `{=…}` etc. Never blank them to `value=""` for “cleaner” markup.
3. **Form contract** — preserve Firstmall `name` / `id` / required hiddens. Restyle with classes/wrappers; do not rename fields the core JS expects.
4. **Live URLs** — links must match Firstmall routes/APIs (e.g. Saved posts → `/mypage/saved_posts`, not `/mypage/myshortform` or prototype paths).
5. **Script path** — prefer `/data/skin/{skin}/app/javascript/js/trendypicker-*.js` so skin uploads are not masked by a stale shared `/app/javascript/...` copy. No `?v=` query strings.

### Shared chrome ownership

| Chrome | Own in | Not by |
|--------|--------|--------|
| My Account LNB | `mypage/mypage_lnb.html` only | Copying `<nav id="mypageLnbBasic">` into each page |
| Customer board LNB | `_modules/common/board_lnb.html` / `{#board_lnb}` | Replacing with My Account nav unless product explicitly requires it |
| Footer | `layout_footer/…` | Inlining full footer into page templates |

```html
<!-- ❌ BAD: inline LNB on every My Page -->
<aside><nav id="mypageLnbBasic">…</nav></aside>

<!-- ✅ GOOD: keep Firstmall include slot -->
<div id="subpageLNB" class="subpage_lnb"><!-- [스킨폴더]/mypage/mypage_lnb.html --></div>
```

## URL → Template

Public URL maps to skin HTML (e.g. `/mypage/wish` → `mypage/wish.html`). Inspect entry + every included module before editing.

## HTML vs CSS vs JS

| Asset | Rule |
|-------|------|
| **HTML** | Edit existing Firstmall templates/modules; keep multi-module split. |
| **CSS** | New `css/redesign/trendypicker-*.css` only — never `common.css` / `user.css`. |
| **JS** | Focused `trendypicker-*.js`; unbind/rebind carefully around Firstmall handlers. |

Do not add `!important` unless a Firstmall ID/legacy rule cannot be beaten with specificity.
Do not append a duplicate selector block in the same file/media context — merge instead.

## Validation

After work-skin edits: `npm run check:firstmall`. Fails on duplicate selectors and `!important` > 25%. Update baselines in `tools/check-css-style.mjs` only after legitimate size/`!important` cleanups.
